  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In an experiment to find out the diameter of wire using screw gauge, the following observation were noted:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0020_e925e3d45a4c.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 146px;\" /></p><p>(a) Screw moves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> on main scale in one complete rotation<br />(b) Total divisions on circular scale <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math><br />(c) Main scale reading is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math><br />(d) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>45</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi></mrow></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mrow><mo>&nbsp;</mo></mrow></msup></math> division of circular scale is in the pitch line<br />(e) Instrument has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> negative error Then the diameter of wire is :</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>",
