  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>From the data given in the question,</p><p>Pitch of the screw gauge<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>.</p><p>Total divisions on the circular scale<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math>.</p><p>Therefore, the least count of the screw gauge is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LC</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mtext>pitch</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MSR</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>CSR</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math></p><p>Diameter reading <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MSR</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>LC</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>CSR</mi><mo>-</mo></math> zero error</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>03</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>98</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
